.TH NV-SYS-TOP 1 "October 2026" "nv-sys-top 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nv-sys-top \- htop-style system monitor with NVIDIA GPUs in the same view
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nv-sys-top
[\fB\-d\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-g\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fIcpu\fR|\fImem\fR|\fIvram\fR|\fIgpu\fR] [\fB\-b\fR [\fB\-n\fR \fIROWS\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nv-sys-top
shows a meter for each CPU core, memory, swap and load, a status block for
every NVIDIA GPU (load, VRAM, temperature, power, fan, SM clock), and one
process list with CPU, RAM, GPU index, per-process GPU load and VRAM.
.PP
System data is read from
.IR /proc .
GPU data comes from NVML
.RI ( libnvidia-ml.so.1 ),
which is loaded at run time. Without it, the GPU part is left out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " SECONDS"
Refresh interval, 0.5 to 10 seconds (default 1.0).
.TP
.B \-g
Show only processes that use a GPU.
.TP
.BI \-s " KEY"
Sort by
.IR cpu ,
.IR mem ,
.I vram
or
.IR gpu .
.TP
.B \-b
Batch mode: print one snapshot as plain text and exit.
.TP
.BI \-n " ROWS"
Number of process rows in batch mode (default 20, 0 for all).
.TP
.B \-h
Show help.
.TP
.B \-V
Show version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B c m g u
Sort by CPU, RAM, VRAM, GPU load.
.TP
.B v
Toggle GPU processes only.
.TP
.B /
Filter by command line; empty input clears the filter.
.TP
.B Up Down PgUp PgDn Home End
Move the cursor. Once moved, the cursor follows its process; Home pins it to the top.
.TP
.B k K
Send SIGTERM or SIGKILL to the selected process, after a y/N prompt.
.TP
.B + \-
Slower or faster refresh.
.TP
.B q Esc
Quit.
.SH FILES
.I /proc/stat /proc/meminfo /proc/loadavg /proc/uptime /proc/[pid]/stat /proc/[pid]/cmdline
.br
.I libnvidia-ml.so.1
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR htop (1),
.BR nvidia-smi (1),
.BR proc (5)
